			<item>
				<title>About</title>
				<link>https://maxwhitney.github.io/deceptive_design_scrape/patterns/about/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://maxwhitney.github.io/deceptive_design_scrape/patterns/about/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;collaborating-to-build-a-safer-more-empowering-online-world-for-everyone&#34;&gt;Collaborating to build a safer, more empowering online world for everyone.&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://maxwhitney.github.io/deceptive_design_scrape/files/Tech_Policy_Design_Lab_Concept_Note.pdf&#34;&gt;Download Concept Note (234kb)&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;alt-text-vision&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://maxwhitney.github.io/deceptive_design_scrape/images/eye-icon.svg&#34; alt=&#34;alt text&#34; title=&#34;Eye Icon&#34;&gt; Vision&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Life today is digital. But far too often the tools and platforms we use create risks and cause harms for many of us. A better digital future is possible when there is constructive collaboration between the people shaping our technology landscape and those using it.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;alt-text-mission&#34;&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://maxwhitney.github.io/deceptive_design_scrape/images/moving-up-icon.svg&#34; alt=&#34;alt text&#34; title=&#34;Moving Up Icon&#34;&gt; Mission&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;We create space for policymakers, tech companies and researchers to learn directly from those affected by technology. Together, we create solutions that limit the worst of humanity and encourage the best online.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Issues</title>
				<link>https://maxwhitney.github.io/deceptive_design_scrape/patterns/issues/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://maxwhitney.github.io/deceptive_design_scrape/patterns/issues/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;issues&#34;&gt;Issues&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://maxwhitney.github.io/deceptive_design_scrape/images/ogbv-feature-p-500.png&#34; alt=&#34;alt text&#34; title=&#34;Woman with locks at a laptop computer&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;helping-end-gender-based-abuse-online&#34;&gt;Helping End Gender-Based Abuse Online&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;The Tech Policy Design Lab pilot focused on creating solutions to counter the abuse of women online. This work led to a group of the world’s biggest tech platforms making specific commitments to take action and improve women’s safety on their platforms.&#xA;[Read more](link to pattern once built)&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://maxwhitney.github.io/deceptive_design_scrape/images/sergey-zolkin-unsplash-feature-p-500.png&#34; alt=&#34;alt text&#34; title=&#34;Hands actively typing on a laptop keyboard&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Playbook - Further Resources</title>
				<link>https://maxwhitney.github.io/deceptive_design_scrape/patterns/playbook/slug-further-resources/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://maxwhitney.github.io/deceptive_design_scrape/patterns/playbook/slug-further-resources/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;further-resources&#34;&gt;Further Resources&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Tech Policy Design Labs bring together governments, companies and civil society in a collaborative environment and use human-centered design thinking to develop policies, processes, or products at the intersection of technology and human rights that come with commitments that are measurable and accountable.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;existing-toolkits-that-are-accessible-to-global-audiences&#34;&gt;Existing Toolkits that are Accessible to Global Audiences&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;a href=&#34;https://airtable.com/appftS8mfXuQCWvhE/shrGMmjLhmkRjfz2i/tblLluPJrFxq0Fi2p?layout=card&#34;&gt;Airtable of Existing Toolkits&lt;/a&gt; &amp;lt;- original page has the airtable embedded; Hugo/cupper doesn&amp;rsquo;t enable airtable embeds easily, so only the link is ported over&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Playbook - Overview</title>
				<link>https://maxwhitney.github.io/deceptive_design_scrape/patterns/playbook/slug-playbook/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://maxwhitney.github.io/deceptive_design_scrape/patterns/playbook/slug-playbook/</guid>
				<description>&lt;p&gt;This is the Playbook pattern subfolder. These are the contents of the &lt;code&gt;playbook.md&lt;/code&gt; file, found in the &lt;code&gt;content\patterns\playbook&lt;/code&gt; folder.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;strong&gt;CONTENT FROM &lt;a href=&#34;https://techpolicydesignlab.webflow.io/playbook&#34;&gt;https://techpolicydesignlab.webflow.io/playbook&lt;/a&gt;&lt;/strong&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h2 id=&#34;tech-policy-design-playbook&#34;&gt;Tech Policy Design Playbook&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;Tech Policy Design Labs bring together governments, companies and civil society in a collaborative environment and use human-centered design thinking to develop policies, processes, or products at the intersection of technology and human rights that come with commitments that are measurable and accountable.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://maxwhitney.github.io/deceptive_design_scrape/images/What-is-a-TPDL-p-1080.jpeg&#34; alt=&#34;alt text&#34; title=&#34;What is Tech Policy Design Lab banner&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
			<item>
				<title>Strategies - Crowdsourced Reporting Tool</title>
				<link>https://maxwhitney.github.io/deceptive_design_scrape/patterns/deceptive-design/slug-strategies-crowdsource/</link>
				<pubDate>Mon, 01 Jan 0001 00:00:00 +0000</pubDate>
				<guid>https://maxwhitney.github.io/deceptive_design_scrape/patterns/deceptive-design/slug-strategies-crowdsource/</guid>
				<description>&lt;h2 id=&#34;create-a-crowdsourced-reporting-tool&#34;&gt;Create a Crowdsourced Reporting Tool&lt;/h2&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;A reporting platform to make Deceptive Design more identifiable, reportable, and trackable for users and regulators.&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;&lt;img src=&#34;https://maxwhitney.github.io/deceptive_design_scrape/images/Banner_CrowdsourceReporting-p-500.jpeg&#34; alt=&#34;alt text&#34; title=&#34;Crowdsource Reporting banner&#34;&gt;&lt;/p&gt;&#xA;&lt;h3 id=&#34;problem&#34;&gt;Problem&lt;/h3&gt;&#xA;&lt;p&gt;There is a lack of visibility regarding the harms associated with Deceptive Design. People on the web do not have a robust enough awareness to identify it, nor a pathway to report it. As a result, policy-makers and regulators lack sufficient evidence to better understand, illustrate, and respond to issues of Deceptive Design.&lt;/p&gt;</description>
			</item>
